  citiesSectionBody: 'Smartious Irish and expat families concentrate across Dublin (South Dublin D4 Ballsbridge/Sandymount, D6 Rathmines/Rathgar, D14 Dundrum/Clonskeagh, D18 Foxrock/Leopardstown — NAISD, SEK, ISD, St. Andrew\'s catchment plus Silicon Docks Google/Meta/LinkedIn corporate), Cork (Apple European HQ Hollyhill + Ireland\'s pharmaceutical cluster Ringaskiddy/Kinsale — Pfizer, Eli Lilly, MSD, Novartis, J&J), Galway (Ireland\'s medtech capital — Medtronic Galway largest global site outside US, Boston Scientific), Limerick (mid-west — Analog Devices, Dell Technologies, Northern Trust, Shannon Free Zone aerospace), Waterford (South East — Bausch + Lomb, Genzyme Sanofi biotech), and Kildare (Intel Ireland Leixlip Fab 34 EUV semiconductor, HPE, Maynooth University). Each city has its own local context — Dublin\'s multinational tech Silicon Docks concentration, Cork\'s Apple + pharma corporate rotation, Galway\'s medtech international curriculum gap-filling, Kildare\'s Intel semiconductor rotation portability — but all share the same live online delivery infrastructure in Irish Standard Time.',

  trustSignals: [
    { h: 'Two operational teaching centres',        p: 'Live teaching to Irish and expat families is delivered from two international-standard operational centres established 2022 and 2023.' },
    { h: 'Morning Ireland delivery',                 p: 'Ireland Standard Time (GMT UTC+0, BST UTC+1 summer). Smartious morning delivery 10 AM – 1 PM Irish time = 1 PM – 4 PM Nairobi EAT teaching — Ireland school-morning window and Nairobi lunchtime teaching hours.' },
    { h: 'Cambridge-registered infrastructure',      p: 'Smartious registers students as private candidates at authorised Cambridge examination venues in Ireland or UK centres. Full administrative handling.' },
    { h: 'Túsla-compatible curriculum provider',     p: 'Irish families withdrawing from formal school register with Túsla (Child and Family Agency) under Education (Welfare) Act 2000 Section 14. Smartious meets Túsla adequacy standard as accredited international curriculum provider delivering Cambridge / IB / American / OSSD qualifications with documented curriculum, contact hours, assessments, and progress reporting suitable for Educational Welfare Officer (EWO) review.' },
  ],

  universitiesInCountry: 'Trinity College Dublin (TCD, established 1592, Ireland\'s oldest and highest-ranked university globally), University College Dublin (UCD, Ireland\'s largest research university), Dublin City University (DCU), Maynooth University (Kildare), University College Cork (UCC), University of Galway (formerly NUI Galway), University of Limerick (UL), Munster Technological University (MTU, Cork), South East Technological University (SETU, Waterford), Technological University Dublin (TU Dublin), plus Royal College of Surgeons in Ireland (RCSI) for medical education. All Irish universities are accessible via CAO (Central Applications Office) for Irish Leaving Cert holders and via international admissions for Cambridge / IB / AP qualification holders.',
  universityChannels: 'Irish universities accept Cambridge A-Level, IB Diploma, and American AP via CAO international admissions channels. TCD, UCD, UCC, University of Galway all published Cambridge / IB / AP conversion tariffs. UK UCAS applications supported through Cambridge A-Level or IB Diploma — particularly relevant for post-Brexit UK family curriculum continuity to UK Russell Group. US Common Application via SAT/ACT + AP portfolios. Canadian OUAC via Ontario OSSD (CCIS partnership) or as international student via Cambridge/IB. Australian direct entry via A-Level or IB. Personalised university guidance sessions with the Head of Academics for target-university strategy across Ireland / UK / US / Canada / Australia destinations.',
  cambridgeCardDescription: 'Smartious\'s primary offer for Irish and expat families. Cambridge IGCSE (Years 10-11) and Cambridge A-Level (Years 12-13) delivered as live online classes with morning Ireland delivery matching Nairobi lunchtime teaching. Private candidate examination registration at authorised Cambridge examination venues in Ireland or UK. Pathway accepted by all Irish universities via CAO, UK Russell Group via UCAS (including Oxbridge for elite candidates), US Ivy League, Canadian U15, Australian Group of Eight.',
  britishCurriculumSuits: 'Irish and expat families targeting Cambridge IGCSE + A-Level pathway. Best fit for: (1) post-Brexit UK families maintaining British curriculum trajectory to UK Russell Group via UCAS, (2) families specifically targeting UK Oxbridge or US Ivy League needing Cambridge / A-Level rather than Irish Leaving Cert, (3) multinational corporate rotational families needing portable curriculum, (4) Túsla-registered Irish homeschool families needing accredited international curriculum.',
  britishCurriculumDelivery: 'Live online classes IST 10 AM – 1 PM (matching Nairobi lunchtime teaching), small groups 4-6 students. Cambridge examinations at authorised Ireland venues or UK centres.',
  ibDiplomaSuits: 'Irish and expat families targeting IB Diploma\'s breadth. NAISD, SEK, St. Andrew\'s College Dublin alternative. Best fit for families targeting US Ivy League, Canadian U15, and holistic university applications.',
  ibDiplomaDelivery: 'Live online IB DP classes across all six subject groups plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay supervision.',
  americanCurriculumSuits: 'Irish and expat families targeting US universities via Common Application. Apple European HQ Cork, Google/Meta Silicon Docks Dublin, Intel Leixlip corporate rotational families with US Common Application university destination alignment.',
  americanCurriculumDelivery: 'American Curriculum with AP courses Grades 9-12, SAT/ACT preparation, Common App essay coaching.',
  founderBioCountrySpecific: 'Alfred Ouko founded Smartious in 2019 to make international qualifications (Cambridge, IB, American, Ontario OSSD) accessible to families across emerging markets and international corporate rotational communities at online-delivery fees. Irish and expat families in Ireland join students in 18 other countries — from Dublin Silicon Docks to Taipei Tianmu, Istanbul Bebek to Cairo Zamalek, Dubai Downtown to Kuala Lumpur Mont Kiara.',
  founderUniversitySpecialism: 'Alfred holds a BEd in Mathematics and Physics — Smartious\'s Cambridge A-Level and IB Diploma STEM subjects are led personally when needed. Head of Academics supervises curriculum delivery and university placement strategy per family across Irish (CAO), UK (UCAS), US (Common App), Canadian (OUAC), and Australian destinations.',

  competitorsIntro: 'Ireland international school fees are relatively affordable compared to Zurich, Geneva, or London but substantial relative to state (free) alternatives. Nord Anglia International School Dublin (NAISD) is the only Ireland school delivering full IB continuum ages 3-18 at EUR 16,000-25,000/year. SEK International School Dublin delivers full IB continuum at EUR 12,000-20,000/year. International School of Dublin (ISD) provides IB PYP ages 3-12 at EUR 12,000-16,000/year. St. Andrew\'s College Booterstown offers dual Irish Leaving Cert + IB Diploma at EUR 7,000-16,000/year. Language-specific schools (St. Kilian\'s Deutsche Schule EUR 4,060/year, Lycée Français d\'Irlande) offer more affordable subsidised options. Selective Irish private day schools (Wesley College, Belvedere College, Blackrock College) range EUR 7,000-10,500/year.',
